{
  "id": "01-pull-the-weeds",
  "title": "Pull the Weeds Early",
  "tenet": "Do not negotiate with sin",
  "durationMs": 67798,
  "text": "Imagine a boy watching his father pull tiny weeds from a vegetable bed. He points to a green shoot and asks, \"Why bother with that little one?\" His father lifts it out between two fingers. Beside the fence, another weed has grown thick and tall. They pull together, but its roots hold fast. When it finally comes loose, it tears up some of the soil around the vegetables. The boy looks from the tangled roots to the tiny shoot in his father's hand. Now he understands why his father did not wait.\n\nDo not negotiate with sin. A resentment, a dishonest excuse, a little envy: what we keep feeding takes root. Taking it seriously means responding early. Tell the truth. Refuse the cruel reply. Bring the temptation to God. If you have already fallen, repent and take the next right step. Remember the two weeds. What you refuse to tend today has less room to grow tomorrow.\n\nToday, name one compromise you have been excusing. Take one concrete step to remove it, and ask God for help. Pull the weeds early.",
